{%- comment -%}
  GOD SQUAD — Empty cart
  Phase 8.

  Accepts:
  - url   {String} optional. The merchant's destination for the button.
  - label {String} optional. The merchant's label for the button.

  Usage:
  {% render 'cart-empty-state', url: section.settings.empty_link, label: section.settings.empty_link_label %}

  Two consumers — the drawer and the cart page — which is why it is a snippet.

  THE DEFAULT DESTINATION IS THE HOME PAGE, NOT /collections/all.
  routes.all_products_collection_url is the obvious answer and it is the wrong
  one in this theme today: no templates/collection.json exists yet, so Shopify
  would serve an error page to every customer who opened an empty cart and
  pressed the one button in it. The home page does exist and carries both the
  New Drop and Best Sellers rows, so it is where a customer with an empty cart
  should land until a collection template ships. The merchant can point it
  anywhere once one does.

  No invented recommendations. The Phase 8 brief rules them out for this phase,
  and there is no recommendation data to draw on in any case.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign empty_url = url
  if empty_url == blank
    assign empty_url = routes.root_url
  endif

  assign empty_label = label
  if empty_label == blank
    assign empty_label = 'cart.empty.link' | t
  endif
-%}

<div class="cart-empty">
  <p class="cart-empty__title">{{ 'cart.empty.title' | t }}</p>
  <p class="cart-empty__body">{{ 'cart.empty.body' | t }}</p>
  <a class="button button--accent" href="{{ empty_url }}">
    {{ empty_label }}
    {% render 'icon-arrow' %}
  </a>
</div>
